# Read CLAUDE.md

`CLAUDE.md`, at the repo root, is the single source of truth for this project:
architecture, roles and auth, the visual and responsive systems, island art and
asset layout, curriculum, project structure, deployment, branching, and the
working rules for agents (§18).

Read it before editing. These rules used to be duplicated across seven
condensed `.mdc` files here, which drifted out of sync with the real doc; they
were folded back into `CLAUDE.md` so there is one place to keep correct.

## The parts you will reach for most

- **§18 Agent Working Rules** — small reversible changes; stop and change
  strategy after 3 failed attempts; never touch `node_modules/`, `dist/`,
  `.vite/`, `package-lock.json`, local IDE settings or the originals in
  `Images/`; run `npm run build` before claiming done; report what changed.
- **§17 Branching** — one branch, `main`. It is protected and auto-deploys, so
  it changes only through a pull request from a short-lived branch.
- **§6 Responsive System** — monitors, Chromebooks (the constraint is *height*),
  phones (the final RESPONSIVE PASS block in `global.css`). Verify at 375×812,
  1366×768 and 1440×900.
- **§6.3 Island art** — one folder per island, path built from the `worldId`.
- **§15 Non-Negotiables** — RBAC, secrets never in `VITE_*`, correct Spanish,
  stable Docker ports, never draw islands or mascots with CSS.

If anything here disagrees with `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE.md` wins.
